    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `title` \u2192 `salutation` feature end-to-end, matching the codebase's existing patterns (derived getters on the entity + OpenAPI-generated DTOs + MapStruct by-name mapping), keeping each concern in its natural home.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of truth for the generated DTOs)\n   - Added an optional `title` string to `OwnerFields` (the request body), documented as one of MR/MRS/MS/DR.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` string to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity)\n   - Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n   - Added a derived `getSalutation()`: `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title \u2014 following the same \"computed getter, never persisted\" convention as `getInitials()`, `getLocality()`, etc.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** (`db/hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `title` column so the JPA entity persists it (tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n4. **`ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT update path) \u2014 copies `title` onto the loaded owner so updates don't silently drop it. The POST/create path needed no change: `BuildOwner` already maps the whole `OwnerFieldsDto` via MapStruct, which picks up `title` by name, and `RespondWithOwner` picks up `salutation` by name.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 GET returns `salutation: \"DR who\"`), and the full suite is green.\n\nI chose a plain `String` for `title` rather than an OpenAPI `enum`: the spec's contract is raw concatenation into `salutation`, and an enum would force a MapStruct enum\u2194String conversion through the mapper and entity for no functional gain. The allowed values are documented in the schema description instead.",
